{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-10258" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,y=2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,t\\in [0,\\pi ].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "59d4e9b0a73d1344d61572859b869d402d7db40a552cde885e09fc038992c02f"} {"question" "q-10258" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)) \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\  & =2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{(2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+{(2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\cdot {\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =2(\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{2}-0) \\\\  & ={\\pi }^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "59d4e9b0a73d1344d61572859b869d402d7db40a552cde885e09fc038992c02f"} {"question" "q-10258" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "15f36d19053e88cb59e92de0eecbef867ff31e7e2a6133fc9aefe0bb07dd1dc0"} {"question" "q-10258" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "59d4e9b0a73d1344d61572859b869d402d7db40a552cde885e09fc038992c02f"} {"question" "q-10258" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{\\pi }^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}"] ["math" "{\\pi }^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "59d4e9b0a73d1344d61572859b869d402d7db40a552cde885e09fc038992c02f"} {"question" "q-10258" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\pi }^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "59d4e9b0a73d1344d61572859b869d402d7db40a552cde885e09fc038992c02f"} {"question" "q-20909" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/assets/59704c6b8e643337113ab99b22eaeaac8d59ac3c15042409e8a0a8eac6ee54fd.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x=\\frac{t}{2},\\,y={e}^{t}$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=1$ (shown above)?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "59d4e9b0a73d1344d61572859b869d402d7db40a552cde885e09fc038992c02f"} {"question" "q-20909" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{t}{2})=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{({e}^{t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{({e}^{2t})+(\\frac{1}{4})}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{4{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "59d4e9b0a73d1344d61572859b869d402d7db40a552cde885e09fc038992c02f"} {"question" "q-20909" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "15f36d19053e88cb59e92de0eecbef867ff31e7e2a6133fc9aefe0bb07dd1dc0"} {"question" "q-20909" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "59d4e9b0a73d1344d61572859b869d402d7db40a552cde885e09fc038992c02f"} {"question" "q-20909" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{4{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{2{e}^{2t}+4}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{t}+4}\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "59d4e9b0a73d1344d61572859b869d402d7db40a552cde885e09fc038992c02f"} {"question" "q-20909" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{4{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "59d4e9b0a73d1344d61572859b869d402d7db40a552cde885e09fc038992c02f"} {"question" "q-21353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/assets/4aa2bca8faab077c47fb968882579233babe7d323ba3120088e8ea5599fbd570.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x={e}^{t},\\,y=t$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=2$ (shown above)?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "59d4e9b0a73d1344d61572859b869d402d7db40a552cde885e09fc038992c02f"} {"question" "q-21353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{({e}^{t})^{2}+(1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "59d4e9b0a73d1344d61572859b869d402d7db40a552cde885e09fc038992c02f"} {"question" "q-21353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "15f36d19053e88cb59e92de0eecbef867ff31e7e2a6133fc9aefe0bb07dd1dc0"} {"question" "q-21353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "59d4e9b0a73d1344d61572859b869d402d7db40a552cde885e09fc038992c02f"} {"question" "q-21353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+4}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}-1}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{e}^{t}+2}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{e}^{t}-1}\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "59d4e9b0a73d1344d61572859b869d402d7db40a552cde885e09fc038992c02f"} {"question" "q-21353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "59d4e9b0a73d1344d61572859b869d402d7db40a552cde885e09fc038992c02f"} {"question" "q-351429" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/assets/5fdcb137c459d5631db3dc3d02ff33ca0b791619694f1badbe7f3f2d0b19141d.png)\n\nFind the arc length $L$ of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,y=\\frac{1}{3}(2t+1)^{3/2},\\,t\\in [0,2].\n$$\n\nDo not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "59d4e9b0a73d1344d61572859b869d402d7db40a552cde885e09fc038992c02f"} {"question" "q-351429" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{3}(2t+1)^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}(2t+1)^{1/2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =(2t+1)^{1/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{(t)^{2}+{((2t+1)^{1/2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{(t+1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}|t+1|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}+t)\\,{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{4}{2}+2)-0 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "59d4e9b0a73d1344d61572859b869d402d7db40a552cde885e09fc038992c02f"} {"question" "q-351429" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "15f36d19053e88cb59e92de0eecbef867ff31e7e2a6133fc9aefe0bb07dd1dc0"} {"question" "q-351429" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "59d4e9b0a73d1344d61572859b869d402d7db40a552cde885e09fc038992c02f"} {"question" "q-351429" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "59d4e9b0a73d1344d61572859b869d402d7db40a552cde885e09fc038992c02f"} {"question" "q-351508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/assets/a61d1a169971b5e0af320372885cdcbae794d163ab767685ef5b688a083aaadb.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=2+4t,\\,y=\\frac{8}{3}{t}^{3/2},\\,t\\in [0,2].\n$$\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "59d4e9b0a73d1344d61572859b869d402d7db40a552cde885e09fc038992c02f"} {"question" "q-351508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2+4t)=4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{8}{3}{t}^{3/2})=4{t}^{1/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{(4{t}^{1/2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{16+16t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{2}(1+t)^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}(1+t)^{3/2}\\,{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}({3}^{3/2}-{1}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}(3\\sqrt{3}-1) \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "59d4e9b0a73d1344d61572859b869d402d7db40a552cde885e09fc038992c02f"} {"question" "q-351508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "15f36d19053e88cb59e92de0eecbef867ff31e7e2a6133fc9aefe0bb07dd1dc0"} {"question" "q-351508" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "59d4e9b0a73d1344d61572859b869d402d7db40a552cde885e09fc038992c02f"} {"question" "q-351508" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{3}(3\\sqrt{3}-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031229/state.json" "file_sha256" "59d4e9b0a73d1344d61572859b869d402d7db40a552cde885e09fc038992c02f"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1210 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
